    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0575" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/39f: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Delegation
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-18T18:00:00-04:00">October 18, 1943—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1012. Amdel No. 20. British Embassy has just informed us that a cable received
                    from the Foreign Office states that the British Government have agreed that the
                    statement on “civil affairs for France”<anchor n="88" xml:id="d565-f1"/> should
                    be “taken as a basis for discussion in Moscow.” (Your Delam no. 2, October
                        15.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d565-f2"/>)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d565-f1" n="88" xml:id="d565-f1-content">
                <p>Conference Document No. 19; for text, see Annex 5 to the Secret Protocol signed
                    at Moscow November 1, 1943, <ref target="#pg760">p. 760</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d565-f2" n="89" xml:id="d565-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; in it the Secretary requested to be informed when concurrence of the
                    British Government on the statement was received from the British Embassy
                    (740.0011 Moscow/29).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
